    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>The region <m>R</m> consists of the points on or inside the triangle with vertices
<m>(-1, -3), (2, -3), (-1, 1)</m>.</p>
<p>(a) The region is bounded below by the line <m>y = -3</m> and above by the line through the points <m>(2, -3), (-1, 1)</m>, which  has
equation <m>y  + 3 = -{\frac{4}{3}} (x - 2)</m>.</p>
<p>The bounds for <m>x</m> are <m>-1 \le x \le 2</m>. Thus 
<me>\iint_R f(x,y) dy\, dx = \int_{-1}^{2} \int_{-3}^{-{\frac{4}{3}}(x-2) - 3} f(x,y) dy dx</me></p>
<p>(b) The region is bounded on the left by the line <m>x = -1</m> and on the right by the line through the points <m>(2, -3), (-1, 1)</m>, which  has
equation <m>x =  -{\frac{3}{4}} (y - 1)  - 1</m>.</p>
<p>The bounds for <m>y</m> are <m>-3 \le x \le 1</m>. Thus 
<me>\iint_R f(x,y) dy\, dx = \int_{-3}^{1} \int_{-1}^{-{\frac{3}{4}}(y-1) - 1} f(x,y) dy dx</me></p>
</solution>
